Job Description - Quality Analyst&nbsp; 

Department: Quality Assurance (QA)&nbsp; 

Industry: Ophthalmic / Eye Care Manufacturing / Contact Lens Care Solutions&nbsp; 

Location: Greater Noida

Reporting To: Head - Quality / Management&nbsp; 

Experience: 2-5 Years (preferably in Ophthalmic or eye care manufacturing)&nbsp; 

Salary: Open for discussion as per the experience

1. Job Purpose&nbsp; 

- We are looking for a detail-oriented and technically competent Quality Analyst to manage and maintain quality documentation, ensure manufacturing and packaging process compliance, and support the implementation of Quality Management Systems (QMS). &nbsp; 
 - The candidate will be responsible for preparing, reviewing and maintaining Batch Manufacturing Records (BMR), Batch Packaging Records (BPR), and other quality-related documents for contact lens solution manufacturing. &nbsp; 
 - The ideal candidate should have a strong understanding of ISO standards, particularly ISO 13485, and European CE regulatory requirements under the Medical Device Regulation (EU MDR 2017/745). &nbsp; 

2. Key Roles & Responsibilities&nbsp; 

A. Batch Documentation & Process Control&nbsp; 

● Prepare, review and maintain Batch Manufacturing Records (BMR) and Batch Packaging Records (BPR). &nbsp; 

● Ensure all manufacturing and packaging activities are documented accurately and in accordance with approved SOPs. &nbsp; 

● Verify batch records for completeness, accuracy, traceability and compliance before batch release. &nbsp; 

● Maintain batch-wise documentation of raw materials, packaging materials, in-process checks and finished goods. &nbsp; 

● Ensure proper documentation of manufacturing parameters, process controls, yields and reconciliation. &nbsp; 

● Review deviations and discrepancies identified during manufacturing and packaging. 

● Maintain batch traceability from raw material procurement to finished product dispatch. &nbsp; 

B. Quality Management System (QMS)&nbsp; 

● Implement, monitor and maintain the company's Quality Management System. 

● Prepare, review and update SOPs, work instructions, quality manuals, formats and other controlled documents. &nbsp; 

● Maintain document control systems, revision history and records. &nbsp; 

● Handle Non-Conformance Reports (NCR), CAPA (Corrective and Preventive Actions), deviations and change control. &nbsp; 

● Coordinate internal quality audits and support external and certification audits. 

● Ensure timely closure of audit observations and implementation of corrective actions. 

● Maintain quality records in accordance with applicable regulatory requirements. &nbsp; 

C. ISO & Regulatory Compliance&nbsp; 

● Ensure compliance with ISO 13485 - Medical Devices Quality Management Systems. &nbsp; 

● Have working knowledge of ISO 9001 and other applicable quality standards. 

● Understand and implement applicable requirements of European Medical Device Regulation (EU MDR 2017/745). &nbsp; 

● Support CE certification activities, including preparation and maintenance of technical documentation. &nbsp; 

● Understand applicable MDR requirements relating to device classification, conformity assessment, labeling, traceability and post-market surveillance. &nbsp; 

● Support compliance with applicable requirements of ISO 14971 - Risk Management for Medical Devices. &nbsp; 

● Coordinate with external auditors, consultants, certification bodies and regulatory agencies as required. &nbsp; 

● Maintain records and documentation required for regulatory inspections and CE audits. &nbsp; 

D. Manufacturing & Quality Assurance&nbsp; 

● Monitor quality compliance across manufacturing, filling, packaging and finished product inspection. &nbsp; 

● Ensure adherence to approved manufacturing procedures and quality standards. 

● Conduct in-process quality checks and verify critical process parameters. 

● Monitor raw material and packaging material quality documentation, including COAs and specifications. &nbsp; 

● Coordinate with production and stores teams to ensure material traceability and quality compliance. &nbsp; 

● Support validation and qualification activities, including process validation, equipment qualification and cleaning validation, as applicable. &nbsp; 

● Monitor environmental conditions and hygiene requirements in manufacturing areas. 

● Assist in investigating product complaints, quality failures and manufacturing deviations. &nbsp; 

E. Testing, Validation & Quality Records&nbsp; 

● Coordinate with internal and external laboratories for raw material, in-process and finished product testing. 

● Maintain records of analytical testing, stability studies and product quality evaluations. &nbsp; 

● Review test reports against approved specifications. &nbsp; 

● Maintain calibration and preventive maintenance records for quality-related equipment. &nbsp; 

● Support preparation and review of product specifications, testing protocols and validation reports. &nbsp; 

3. Required Qualifications & Experience&nbsp; 

● B. Sc. / M. Sc. in Chemistry, Microbiology, Biotechnology or related scientific discipline. 

● B. Pharm / M. Pharm or equivalent qualification will also be considered. 

● 2-5 years of experience in Quality Assurance / Quality Control in pharmaceutical, medical device or healthcare manufacturing. &nbsp; 

● Prior experience in preparing and reviewing BMR, BPR and quality documentation is essential. &nbsp; 

● Practical exposure to ISO 13485 implementation and audit requirements. 

● Good understanding of CE certification and EU MDR 2017/745 requirements. &nbsp; 

4. Technical Skills & Competencies&nbsp; 

The candidate must have: &nbsp; 

● Strong knowledge of ISO 13485 and Quality Management Systems. 

● Working knowledge of EU MDR 2017/745 and CE compliance requirements. 

● Experience in preparation, review and maintenance of BMR and BPR. 

● Knowledge of SOP preparation, document control and record management. 

● Understanding of CAPA, NCR, deviation management and change control. 

● Knowledge of risk management and validation documentation. &nbsp; 

● Familiarity with manufacturing quality controls and batch traceability. 

● Strong analytical, documentation and problem-solving skills. &nbsp; 

● Good working knowledge of MS Excel, Word and documentation systems. 

5. Preferred Skills&nbsp; 

● Experience in contact lens solutions, ophthalmic products, medical liquids or sterile/ non-sterile liquid manufacturing. &nbsp; 

● Exposure to medical device technical file preparation. &nbsp; 

● Knowledge of ISO 14971 risk management. &nbsp; 

● Experience in internal and external quality audits. &nbsp; 

● Familiarity with microbiological testing, preservative efficacy testing and stability studies. &nbsp; 

● Understanding of product labeling and packaging compliance. &nbsp; 

● Exposure to supplier qualification and vendor quality management. 

6. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)&nbsp; 

The candidate will be evaluated on: &nbsp; 

1. Accuracy and completeness of BMR and BPR documentation. &nbsp; 

2. Timely review and closure of batch documentation. &nbsp; 

3. Compliance with ISO 13485 and applicable MDR requirements. &nbsp; 

4. Timely preparation, review and updating of SOPs and quality documents. 

5. Reduction in documentation errors and non-conformities. &nbsp; 

6. Timely closure of CAPA and audit observations. &nbsp; 

7. Successful completion of internal and external quality audits. &nbsp; 

8. Maintenance of complete batch traceability and quality records. &nbsp; 

9. Timely coordination of testing, validation and quality compliance activities. 

7. Ideal Candidate Profile&nbsp; 

- Experience in Ophthalmic or Eye Care Manufacturing will be preferred. 
 - The ideal candidate should be hands-on and capable of independently managing quality documentation and compliance activities in a manufacturing environment. &nbsp; 
 - We are looking for someone who understands not just the preparation of quality documents but also the practical implementation of quality systems on the factory floor. &nbsp; 
 - The candidate should be proactive, detail-oriented, disciplined in documentation and capable of coordinating effectively with Production, Purchase, Stores, Finance and external regulatory consultants. &nbsp; 
 - Most importantly, the candidate should have practical knowledge of ISO 13485 and EU MDR requirements, rather than merely theoretical familiarity with these standards. &nbsp;

Roboyo&nbsp; AI&nbsp; is a category shaper in Applied AI and Agentic Automation. &nbsp; We help leading enterprises move from automation projects and AI experiments into governed, production-grade systems that execute real work across workflows, processes, &nbsp; products&nbsp; and services. &nbsp; 

Our heritage is in scaled enterprise automation; our future is&nbsp; Applied AI and&nbsp; Agentic&nbsp; Automation: autonomous agents, AI engineering squads, process orchestration, data and knowledge foundations, and human-in-the-loop governance embedded deeply into how our clients&nbsp; operate. &nbsp; 

We are not here to sell AI theatre. We are here to turn AI into&nbsp; working systems, measurable&nbsp; outcomes&nbsp; and repeatable transformation programs. &nbsp; 

