Spreetail propels brands to increase their ecommerce market share across the globe while improving their operational costs. Learn how we are building one of the fastest-growing ecommerce companies in history: www. spreetail. com. &nbsp; 

Our Phoenix team builds the product catalog and channel integrations that publish Spreetail's listings to marketplaces such as Amazon and Walmart, along with AI-assisted tools that improve listing content and images at scale. We're looking for a Senior Software Engineer who designs scalable, reliable systems, builds dependable features on top of LLMs, and lifts the engineers around them. If you are looking for an environment that provides creative freedom, work-life balance, and meaningful relationships, keep scrolling. &nbsp; 

What we offer: 

- Fully remote work - work from anywhere in India, with the creative freedom and work-life balance to do your best work

- Very competitive salary - we benchmark aggressively to attract top engineering talent. &nbsp; 

- Industry-leading health coverage - health insurance up to ₹30 Lakh, covering you, your family, and your parents. &nbsp; 

- Generous paid leave - a time-off policy that lets you truly recharge and prioritize your wellbeing. &nbsp; 

- Employer of Record (EOR) engagement - we handle payroll and tax compliance so you don't have to. &nbsp; 

How you will achieve success: 

- Own our AI-assisted catalog services end to end, from design through production monitoring, alerting and runbooks. &nbsp; 

- Lead system design for scale, idempotency, failure recovery and data consistency across catalog, channels and asynchronous workers. &nbsp; 

- Build dependable LLM features: design prompts and structured outputs, validate responses against source data, measure quality, latency and cost, and catch regressions before changes ship. &nbsp; 

- Learn and improve our . NET catalog, offer and channel services, and build reliable integrations with marketplace APIs. &nbsp; 

- Use AI coding tools to deliver faster, and review AI-generated code critically before it reaches production. &nbsp; 

- Work directly with US stakeholders, turn ambiguous problems into clear plans, and communicate progress and risks early. &nbsp; 

- Mentor engineers, raise the bar through design and code reviews, and take part in a follow-the-sun on-call rotation. &nbsp; 

- Stay hands-on: write high-quality, maintainable, well-tested code. &nbsp; 

What experiences will help you in this role: 

- 7+ years of backend software engineering experience building and operating production services. &nbsp; 

- Deep system design and distributed systems expertise: queues, concurrency, idempotency, retries, partial failure, consistency and scaling. &nbsp; 

- Has shipped and run at least one AI/LLM-powered system in production for a year or more, and solved real problems on it: prompt design, structured output validation, error and rate-limit handling, and cost control. &nbsp; 

- Experience measuring LLM output quality with test sets or evaluations, not just spot checks. &nbsp; 

- Strong in at least one backend language (Python, C#, Java or similar). Python is a plus; willingness to work in both Python and . NET is a must. &nbsp; 

- Strong code-review skills: you can read a change you didn't write and spot correctness, edge-case and scaling problems. &nbsp; 

- Strong SQL and data modeling, and experience with message brokers such as RabbitMQ or SQS. &nbsp; 

- Strong with cloud infrastructure (AWS or Azure), containers and Kubernetes, CI/CD and observability. &nbsp; 

- A track record of technical leadership: mentoring engineers, influencing design and setting engineering standards. &nbsp; 

- Excellent communication, the ability to work independently with US stakeholders, and availability for about four hours of daily overlap with US Central time, especially in your first 90 days. &nbsp; 

- Nice-to-have: hands-on . NET, ecommerce catalog or marketplace integrations (Amazon SP-API, Walmart), Amazon Bedrock, Snowflake and load testing. &nbsp; 

What to expect: 

Three one-hour technical interviews (problem solving, low-level design and high-level design), followed by a conversation with engineering leadership. &nbsp; 

