Reinvent your world. We are building a modern Wipro. We are an end-to-end digital transformation partner with the boldest ambitions. To realize them, we need people inspired by reinvention. Of yourself, your career, and your skills. We want to see the constant evolution of our business and our industry. It has always been in our DNA - as the world around us changes, so do we. Join a business powered by purpose and a place that empowers you to design your own reinvention.

General Manager - Technical & Plant Operations&nbsp; 

MetaLoop Renewables Private Limited | Kharagpur, West Bengal | Full-time, on-site&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

We're building greater capability to recover, refine and reintegrate materials. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

Our new battery recycling and lead refining facility in Kharagpur is an important step towards a larger, more capable material recovery business. With new infrastructure and technology comes the need for stronger teams, clearer responsibilities and consistent ways of working. 

We're looking for a hands-on technical leader to help shape that next stage. As General Manager, you'll bring together lead metallurgy, customer requirements, regulatory responsibilities and day-to-day plant operations. 

You'll help teams understand what good work looks like, make informed decisions and take ownership of the outcome. Your contribution will matter both in the material we supply and in the capability we build within our people. 

&nbsp; 

What you'll own&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

Government and regulatory liaison&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

1. Represent the unit in technical discussions with the West Bengal Pollution Control Board and other relevant government departments. 

2. Coordinate inspections, oversee technical submissions and responses to queries, and follow through on permit conditions and compliance actions. 

&nbsp; 

Customer specifications and product development&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

1. Work directly with customers to understand their requirements for refined lead and lead alloys. 

2. Assess whether the plant can consistently meet the required composition and impurity limits, and lead trials, technical approvals and follow-up on quality complaints. 

&nbsp; 

Shop-floor SOP compliance&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

1. Ensure approved standard operating procedures are understood and followed across both shifts. 

2. Set clear expectations, verify compliance on the floor, investigate deviations and check that corrective actions are working. 

3. Help build consistency through proper documentation and communication between teams. 

&nbsp; 

What you'll bring&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

1. Ideally, 15+ years of relevant experience, including at least 5 years in a technical leadership role and substantial direct experience in lead refining or lead alloy manufacturing. &nbsp; 

2. A BE/B. Tech in Metallurgical Engineering is preferred. Candidates with a degree in Mechanical or Chemical Engineering will also be considered. &nbsp; 

3. Hands-on knowledge of lead metallurgy, process control and quality testing, including interpreting spectrometer results and troubleshooting off-spec batches. &nbsp; 

4. Experience dealing directly with pollution control boards or other industrial regulators, including handling inspections and explaining plant processes and controls. &nbsp; 

5. Experience taking a customer-specific product from technical discussion through trials, approval and regular supply. &nbsp; 

6. A track record of implementing SOPs in a round-the-clock plant. Commissioning or ramp-up experience is preferred. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

Building the next stage together&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

Professionalism, responsibility and clarity guide the organisation we're building. We value practical knowledge, clear communication and people who see their decisions through. 

This is an opportunity to help establish how a new facility works, develop the team around it and build operations that customers and colleagues can depend on as we grow. 

&nbsp; 

To apply, send your CV to admin@metalooprenewables. com. &nbsp;

